{"records":[{"id":"65pfcj4j4m","title":"Protocol of CRISPR-Cas9 knockout screens for identifying ferroptosis regulators","description":"Ferroptosis, an iron-dependent programmed cell death triggered by excessive lipid peroxidation, has shown promising therapeutic potentials in human diseases. Here, we describe a protocol of a CRISPR-Cas9 loss-of-function screen to identify regulators in response to different inducers of ferroptosis. We emphasize the steps of library amplification, drug treatment, high-throughput sequencing preparation, and bioinformatics analysis using Model-based Analysis of Genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 Knockout (MAGeCK). We also present a method to discover the regulators of ferroptosis and verify the potential targets efficiently.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-10-24T01:46:48.793Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/65pfcj4j4m","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/65pfcj4j4m"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xin","last_name":"Yang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wei","last_name":"Gu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR/Cas9","Ferroptosis"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"835fcfbvhs","title":"Preparation of CRISPR/Cas9 and gRNA plasmids","description":"Human genome engineering has been transformed by the introduction of the CRISPR (clustered regularly interspaced short palindromic repeats)/Cas (CRISPR-associated) system found in most bacteria and archaea. Type II CRISPR/Cas systems have been engineered to induce RNA-guided genome editing in human cells, where small RNAs function together with Cas9 nucleases for sequence-specific cleavage of target sequences. Here we describe the protocol for Cas9-mediated human genome engineering, including construct building and transfection methods necessary for delivering Cas9 and guide RNA (gRNA) into human-induced pluripotent stem cells (hiPSCs) and HEK293 cells. Following genome editing, we also describe methods to assess genome editing effi- ciency using next-generation sequencing and isolate monoclonal hiPSCs with the desired modifications for downstream applications. Keywords: genome engineering • CRISPR • human stem cells","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2016-12-12T12:58:15.307Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/835fcfbvhs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/835fcfbvhs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"George","last_name":"Church","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Experimental Method"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"z4ht3txn2k","title":"Accompanying Files for paper entitled: \"Genome-scale mapping of DNA damage suppressors through phenotypic CRISPR/Cas9 screens\" - Zhao et al. Molecular Cell 2023","description":"Accompanying Files for paper entitled: \"Genome-scale mapping of DNA damage suppressors through phenotypic CRISPR/Cas9 screens\" - Zhao et al. Molecular Cell 2023. This dataset contains Source and additional Data for all figures.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-06-06T07:16:19.286Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/z4ht3txn2k","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/z4ht3txn2k"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Daniel","last_name":"Durocher","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Yichao","last_name":"Zhao","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01gavpb45","name":"Canadian Institutes of Health Research","grant_id":null}],"categories":["DNA Replication","DNA Repair","Flow Cytometry","Cancer Chemotherapy","DNA Damage","Functional Genomics","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"33tm3dd9dw","title":"FAME-CRISPR: Improved CRISPR-Cas9 Genome Editing via HDAC Inhibition and Engineered Virus-Like Particle Delivery ","description":"Raw data deposited for \"FAME-CRISPR: Improved CRISPR-Cas9 Genome Editing via HDAC Inhibition and Engineered Virus-Like Particle Delivery\" by Djamshidi et al-Cell Reports Methods","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-09-25T15:53:30.358Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/33tm3dd9dw","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/33tm3dd9dw"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mahbod","last_name":"Djamshidi","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Sanger Sequencing","Immunofluorescence"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"3ctpx4k6jp","title":"Porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus upregulates SMPDL3B to promote viral replication by modulating lipid metabolism","description":"We generated a collection of porcine genome-scale CRISPR/Cas9 knockout (PigGeCKO) cells on a PAM background.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-06-26T18:53:54.241Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3ctpx4k6jp","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3ctpx4k6jp"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"huanh","last_name":"Shen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Agricultural Biotechnology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"pv8t3hbg4t","title":"Proteasome-Bound UCH37 Debranched Ubiquitin Chains to Promote Degradation. Deol et al. ","description":"The following documents show sequencing data confirming CRISPR/Cas9 genome editing of cell lines, all gels used for analysis, and mass spectrometric chromatograms and LC traces. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-10-09T23:09:46.22Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/pv8t3hbg4t","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/pv8t3hbg4t"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Eric","last_name":"Strieter","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kirandeep","last_name":"Deol","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Sean","last_name":"Crowe","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jiale","last_name":"Du","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Heather ","last_name":"Bisbee","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Robert","last_name":"Guenette","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Mass Spectrometry","Gel","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"xvk2gk4hw3","title":"Data of Murine Trophoblast Organoids as a Model for Trophoblast Development and CRISPR/Cas9 Screening","description":"Raw data for figures in Murine Trophoblast Organoids as a Model for Trophoblast Development and CRISPR/Cas9 Screening","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-10-25T15:27:04.321Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xvk2gk4hw3","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xvk2gk4hw3"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Qian","last_name":"Mao","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Developmental Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"vs9fwhbcvj","title":"Genome-wide Brie CAD5 Surface PrPC - Differentiated PrPC High","description":"These are the raw .fastq files from NGS runs of the genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 KO library (Brie) performed in differentiated CAD5 cells.  They are labeled Brie_PrPC_High to indicate that these sgRNA sequences were captured in the \"PrPC High\" populations during FACS.  Bioinformatic analysis was performed using the MAGeCK-VISPR and MAGeCKFlute pipelines using the biological replicates function to compare between \"PrP Low\" and \"PrP High\" samples.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-13T07:36:42.171Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/vs9fwhbcvj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/vs9fwhbcvj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"P20-GM113132 "},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"}],"categories":["Prion","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"p5t6d78zn8","title":"Genome-wide Brie CAD5 Surface PrPC - Differentiated PrPC Low","description":"These are the raw .fastq files from NGS runs of the genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 KO library (Brie) performed in differentiated CAD5 cells.  They are labeled Brie_PrPC_Low  to indicate that these sgRNA sequences were captured in the \"PrPC Low\" populations during FACS.  Bioinformatic analysis was performed using the MAGeCK-VISPR and MAGeCKFlute pipelines using the biological replicates function to compare between \"PrP Low\" and \"PrP High\" samples.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-13T07:36:58.456Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/p5t6d78zn8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/p5t6d78zn8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"P20-GM113132 "},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"}],"categories":["Prion","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"hzr4fnvc88","title":"Rapid two-step target capture ensures efficient CRISPR-Cas9-guided genome editing. Shi, Al-Sayyad, & Wasko et al.","description":"Raw experimental data from experiments detailed in \"Rapid two-